---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const guides = (await getCollection('guides')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---
<DocsLayout title="Get help with OpenTubeX" description="Install the app, bring your subscriptions with you, and make OpenTubeX your own.">
  <p>New to OpenTubeX? Start with <a href="/docs/installing/">installation</a>, then <a href="/docs/getting-started/">subscribe to your first channel</a>. You can browse and build a local library without a YouTube account.</p>
  <div class="docs-topics">
    {guides.map((guide) => (
      <a class="docs-topic" href={`/docs/${guide.id}/`} aria-label={guide.data.title}>
        <h2>{guide.data.title}</h2>
        <p>{guide.data.description}</p>
        <span aria-hidden="true">Read guide →</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>These guides use the English interface labels. Screenshots show the desktop app; the Android preview uses a smaller-screen layout and some features differ. Your installed version may look different.</p>
  <p>Looking for a feature overview? See <a href="/extra-features/">Features</a>. For changes between versions, read the <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
